BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-mon-speedA@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T120000
SUMMARY:P225 · Speed A · Overspeed\, no ball
DESCRIPTION:Do this before Gym 1\, while the nervous system is fresh. Ev
 ery swing is max intent.\n\nWarm-up 8 min: 90/90s\, open-books\, leg sw
 ings\, then 10 progressive swings from 60% to 90%.\nOverspeed round = l
 ight 5/5/5\, medium 5/5/5\, heavy 5/5/5 (dominant side / non-dominant s
 ide / step-through). Rest 60–90 s between sets.\nBlock 1: 2 rounds (9
 0 swings). Note the peak speed at each weight.\nFinisher: 10 max-effort
  driver swings on the radar. Record the peak club speed.\nWith the Stac
 k: follow the app's prescribed session instead of the fixed rounds — 
 it periodizes the weights for you.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed A · Overspeed\, no ball
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed A · Overspeed\, no ball
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-mon-gym1@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260914T131000
SUMMARY:P225 · Gym 1 · Lower strength + vertical power
DESCRIPTION:Squat pattern\, hinge\, single-leg\, lateral push-off. Verti
 cal force is the biggest single lever on club speed.\n\nA1 Box jump or 
 countermovement jump — 4×3\nA2 Hang power clean — Technique 3×3\,
  light (optional)\nB Back squat — 4×6 @ 72–77%\nC Romanian deadlif
 t — 3×8\nD1 Rear-foot-elevated split squat — 3×8 / leg\nD2 Latera
 l lunge or Cossack squat — 3×8 / side\nE1 Pallof press — 3×10 / s
 ide\nE2 Suitcase carry — 3×30 m / side
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 1 · Lower strength + vertical power
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 1 · Lower strength + vertical power
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-tue-gym2@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260915T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260915T123500
SUMMARY:P225 · Gym 2 · Upper strength + rotational power
DESCRIPTION:Throws first while you're fresh\, then press and pull heavy\
 , then the rotational cable work that builds the release.\n\nA1 Med bal
 l rotational scoop throw (wall) — 4×4 / side · 8–10 lb\nA2 Med ba
 ll chest pass / shot put — 4×4 · 8–10 lb\nB Bench press — 4×6 
 @ 72–77%\nC Weighted pull-up — 4×6\nD1 Half-kneeling landmine pres
 s — 3×8 / side\nD2 Chest-supported row — 3×10\nE1 Cable chop and 
 lift — 3×10 / side\nE2 Face pull — 3×15\nE3 Wrist roller or plate
  pinch — 3 sets
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 2 · Upper strength + rotational power
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 2 · Upper strength + rotational power
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-wed-speedB@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T121000
SUMMARY:P225 · Speed B · Overspeed + hitting
DESCRIPTION:Range or net with the radar. Half technique\, half intent. T
 his is where club speed becomes ball speed.\n\nWarm-up 10 min: mobility
 \, 10 wedge swings\, 10 7-iron swings\, 6 driver at 80%.\nOverspeed: 1 
 round\, light and medium only.\n12 drivers at 85–90%: foot spray or i
 mpact tape on the face\, find centre contact. Smash factor is your feed
 back (target 1.48–1.50).\n3 × 6-ball sets at max intent\, 3 min betw
 een sets. Record peak ball speed\, peak club speed\, and smash.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed B · Overspeed + hitting
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed B · Overspeed + hitting
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-thu-gym3@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260917T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260917T124000
SUMMARY:P225 · Gym 3 · Lower hypertrophy + posterior chain
DESCRIPTION:Deadlift day. Horizontal and lateral jumps up front\, then t
 he volume that builds glutes and hamstrings.\n\nA1 Broad jump — 4×3\
 nA2 Lateral bound (stick the landing) — 4×3 / side\nB Trap bar deadl
 ift — 4×6 @ 72–77%\nC Front squat (or hack squat) — 3×8–10\nD
 1 Barbell hip thrust — 3×10\nD2 Nordic curl or lying leg curl — 3
 ×8\nE1 Copenhagen plank — 3×30 s / side\nE2 Standing calf raise —
  3×12\nE3 Farmer carry — 3×40 m
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 3 · Lower hypertrophy + posterior chain
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 3 · Lower hypertrophy + posterior chain
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-sat-speedC@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260919T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260919T115000
SUMMARY:P225 · Speed C · Max hit day
DESCRIPTION:The session that produces the number. Friday is a rest day s
 o you arrive fresh. Every ball on the radar.\n\nWarm-up 15 min: mobilit
 y\, 20 progressive swings wedge → 7-iron → driver\, 6 drivers at 80
 –90%.\n4 × 6-ball sets on a 2:45 clock\, 5 min rest between sets. Lo
 g every ball speed\; the session number is your peak\, and note the top
 -3 average.\nStop rule: if a set's average drops more than 3% below you
 r best set\, the session is over. Speed under fatigue is where obliques
  and backs get hurt.\nCap: 30 max-effort hits. Then Gym 4 at least 3 ho
 urs later.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed C · Max hit day
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Speed C · Max hit day
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:w1-sat-gym4@project225
DTSTAMP:20260908T154719Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260919T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260919T175500
SUMMARY:P225 · Gym 4 · Upper hypertrophy + arms/grip
DESCRIPTION:After the max hit day (3+ hours later\, or that evening). Pu
 re mass work — shoulders\, back\, arms\, forearms. Nothing here shoul
 d feel heroic.\n\nB Push press (or strict overhead press) — 4×8\nC L
 at pulldown or pull-up — 4×8–10\nD1 Incline dumbbell press — 3×
 10\nD2 Seated cable row — 3×10–12\nE1 Lateral raise — 3×15\nE2 
 Rear delt fly — 3×15\nF1 Hammer curl — 3×12\nF2 Triceps pushdown 
 — 3×12\nF3 Reverse curl + wrist curl — 3×12 each
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 4 · Upper hypertrophy + arms/grip
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:P225 · Gym 4 · Upper hypertrophy + arms/grip
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
